This is the first release of the IHP__MPC9639 "Chipalooza" harness chip.
This is a mixed-signal multi-project carrier design.

The general design is a 64-pin die that is divided into 18 sections
for analog and mixed-signal projects.  Each section is provided resources
of

(1) A switched power supply
(2) Shared digital power supply
(3) Shared ground lines
(4) One voltage bias line
(5) Two current bias lines
(6) Digital control inputs and digital status outputs

At the bottom of the design is a small digital controller for
interfacing to an external host computer through an SPI
interface (with the intent to use a USB-to-SPI interface such
as an FTDI chip).  The SPI interface is a standard 4-pin
interface and matches the Efabless Caravel chip housekeeping
SPI definition for the controls, with internal registers for
control output and status input from the project areas.

The chip is generated from the original open source repository
which can be found at

    https://github.com/RTimothyEdwards/sg13cmos5l_ocd_chipalooza

The state of the repository at tapeout with the project slots
populated with user projects is preserved in the git branch

    tapeout_nov_2026

The chip is constructed according to the Makefile process in that
repository and the 18 projects recorded in the "config.txt" file.
Design files and final data are copied to this tapeout repository
after a completed build.  Please see the original repository for
additional information.
